1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,540
Floating on the Nakagawa, aiming for Kasuga,

2
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and even my shoe flew off.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,900
Onto the head of the
carpenter I had in a chokehold,

4
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I was still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I chase some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:46,100
Katsushika Kameari

7
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,280
even a single yawn changes nothing.

8
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,180
The streetscape is strangely gentle.

9
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed hat's water canteen,

10
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:07,460
great shaku, heaven's source,
the sunset falls.

11
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too, it'll end just like this

12
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
Katsushika Shibamata,
losing happiness once again.

13
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:24,600
Because I'm a fool who finally realized it.

14
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:31,320
Passionate Love: Ryo-chan and Maria

15
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:37,660
Idiot!

16
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:41,680
Do you have no sense of
responsibility as a working adult?

17
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:43,700
I'm sick of lecturing you.

18
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:45,860
If you're sick of it,
you don't have to do it.

19
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:47,100
As if I'd let that happen.

20
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,020
You're late every single time.

21
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:54,540
Look at me. My commute takes two and a half hours,
yet I've never once been late.

22
00:01:54,540 --> 00:01:56,840
That's because you have
someone to wake you up, Chief.

23
00:01:57,380 --> 00:01:58,980
I'm a single man, you know.

24
00:01:59,580 --> 00:02:01,060
Like that's something to brag about.

25
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:03,100
Then why don't you get married?

26
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:03,900
Marriage?

27
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:09,360
That's right, this is the only way to
completely reform your attitude and lifestyle.

28
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:14,280
You'll get married, have kids,
buy a house, and become a proper family man.

29
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:16,140
Family man?

30
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:18,740
Well, I'm off.

31
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,920
No way, you're joking.

32
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:25,200
I have no intention of getting married.

33
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:27,180
You'll do it whether you intend to or not.

34
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:30,160
No, I'll get you married no matter what.

35
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:31,960
I'll never do it, no way.

36
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:32,960
Marriage!

37
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:33,520
I won't.

38
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:35,320
Marriage, marriage, marriage!

39
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:36,860
I won't, I won't, I won't!

40
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:47,960
Me, a devoted family man?

41
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:50,540
Just imagining it gives me the creeps.

42
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:55,880
Why isn't he coming out?

43
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:02,420
I'm sorry.

44
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:09,700
Let's end this chase game already.

45
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:12,660
All I want is for you
to go on a date with me.

46
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:13,600
Let go!

47
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:19,140
Tasty? Tasty?

48
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:20,260
Who the hell do you think you are?

49
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:22,740
You step on someone and then talk like that?
That's uncalled for.

50
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:24,640
That's important

51
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:26,560
Before I die, one last thing.

52
00:03:27,060 --> 00:03:28,220
I'm going to die.

53
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:29,700
That's not cool.

54
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:32,660
Damn you, you'll pay for this!

55
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,460
Don't run, let me hit you some more.

56
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:38,460
Thank you very much.

57
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:40,420
Besides, you too...

58
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:50,600
Sorry for the trouble.

59
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:51,954
W-well, no,

60
00:03:52,004 --> 00:03:55,120
I was just doing what any
police officer should do.

61
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:56,400
What's your name?

62
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:57,920
Me? Me?

63
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:01,100
Well, I'm from the
Kameari Kōen-mae police box,

64
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:02,500
and I'm Kankichi Ryotsu!

65
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,500
Ryotsu from the Kameari Kōen-mae police box.

66
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:06,020
Yes.

67
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,540
I'm Asato Ai.

68
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:10,680
Asato Ai?

69
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:14,040
Asato is "village of morning,
" and Ai is the "ai" of love.

70
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:17,660
Please, just call me Mi-mi-a.

71
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:19,020
Maria.

72
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:20,940
Yes, Ryo-sama.

73
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:30,188
Maria Ahh,

74
00:04:30,238 --> 00:04:33,860
I'm so lucky to get to know such a beauty!

75
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:42,400
You set a trap for Ryo-chan?

76
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,380
Okay, you're talking too loudly.

77
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:47,760
Even if we arrange a regular omiai meeting,

78
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:50,240
Ryotsu would never show up obediently,
you know.

79
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:51,780
Well, to put it simply,

80
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:54,640
it's a plan to turn
Ryotsu into a family man.

81
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:57,940
I'm not falling for some
trap set by a mere chief!

82
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,380
Senpai, what should we have for lunch?

83
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:03,760
Let me see.

84
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:05,640
How about some ramen
from Tsurukame Prefecture?

85
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:06,800
Excuse me.

86
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:11,420
Is there a man here named Kankichi Ryotsu?

87
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:23,400
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

88
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:24,700
Just an acquaintance.

89
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:26,820
So, what are you doing here?

90
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:29,820
I came to make lunch to
thank you for earlier.

91
00:05:30,660 --> 00:05:31,460
Whoa...

92
00:05:33,780 --> 00:05:35,420
This is awesome!

93
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:38,060
Alright, then. Let's eat!

94
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:40,241
Delicious,

95
00:05:40,291 --> 00:05:43,080
too delicious!

96
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:44,920
I'm so glad.

97
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:49,160
Did it suit your taste?
May I come and cook for you again?

98
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:51,800
Yeah, I'd welcome such
delicious food any time!

99
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:56,700
I'd love to keep making Ryo-san's lunches.

100
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:01,680
Ryo-san, then see you tomorrow!

101
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:02,900
Yeah, I'll be waiting!

102
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:10,000
Phew, I guess I won't have
to worry about lunch anymore

103
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:10,800
Senpai.

104
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,420
What are you being so carefree about?

105
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:15,660
Wanting to cook for you every day means
I want to be by your side forever.

106
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:18,140
In other words, I want to marry you, Senpai.

107
00:06:18,140 --> 00:06:19,140
M-marry?

108
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:22,380
N-no way.

109
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,380
There's no mistake about it.

110
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:27,400
Beautiful, polite, and an amazing cook.

111
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,360
She's truly the ideal bride.

112
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:30,880
Bride?

113
00:06:31,340 --> 00:06:33,260
Senpai, you really pulled it off.

114
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:35,480
For such a wonderful person to fall for you.

115
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:37,380
You'll propose right away, of course, right?

116
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:38,700
Propose?

117
00:06:39,020 --> 00:06:40,580
You two will be a perfect match.

118
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:41,320
Yeah, yeah.

119
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:45,100
Me and Maria, getting married?

120
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:54,700
Uunnh...

121
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:59,960
So now you're joining the
ranks of family men too, senpai.

122
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:02,820
Yeah, well, it's not decided yet, you know.

123
00:07:02,820 --> 00:07:06,200
Family man... speaking of which,

124
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:08,580
they set a trap for Ryotsu.

125
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,420
No way, Maria...

126
00:07:10,420 --> 00:07:12,680
No, it's true, this is all too convenient.

127
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:14,820
Going out of their way to pick
on me right in front of me...

128
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:16,500
And then it even reaches Reiko.

129
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:18,980
And these guys' attitude...

130
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:29,180
I see, so that's how it was.

131
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:39,680
Maria is a nice girl, that's for sure.

132
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:42,660
But the problem is that
she's the Chief's acquaintance.

133
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:46,960
If I married a girl like that, I'd be stuck with
the Chief hounding me for the rest of my life.

134
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:49,260
Shh, Kana, Kanakana.

135
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:54,040
Ryo-sama!

136
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:58,420
Ryo-sama!

137
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:01,880
Maria!

138
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:04,700
Maria!

139
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:06,880
Ryo-sama, from now on,

140
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:10,000
you're going to become a serious family man!

141
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,760
Chief!

142
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:14,240
Stop it, let go, stop it!

143
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:15,220
Ryo-sama!

144
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,376
Help! Stop it, please,

145
00:08:19,426 --> 00:08:22,040
Chief! Don't bring your face so close!

146
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:23,820
Ryo-sama, Ryo-sama!

147
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:27,780
What's the matter, Ryo-sama?

148
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:30,480
Ugh, I had a terrible dream.

149
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:31,820
What kind of dream was it?

150
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:35,120
I thought it was Maria,
but it was actually the Chief...

151
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:37,960
Why are you here, Maria!

152
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:38,874
Of course,

153
00:08:38,924 --> 00:08:42,220
I came to make breakfast for you, Ryo-sama.

154
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:43,800
Huh?

155
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:47,520
Mm.

156
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:48,080
Mm.

157
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:53,300
Mm...

158
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:54,720
Mm...

159
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:54,780
Mm...

160
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:55,440
Mm...

161
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:55,900
Mm...

162
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:56,360
Mm...

163
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:56,540
Mm...

164
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:56,920
Mm...

165
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:57,360
Mm...

166
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:57,420
Mm...

167
00:08:57,420 --> 00:08:57,660
Mm...

168
00:08:57,660 --> 00:08:59,160
Ow...

169
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:02,140
Now then, Ryo-sama.

170
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:04,940
That looks good. Well then, let's dig in.

171
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:05,647
This won't do.

172
00:09:05,697 --> 00:09:10,240
If I keep going like this,
I'll get dragged along at her pace.

173
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:14,278
Ha ha I walked right into the trap,
didn't I?

174
00:09:14,328 --> 00:09:15,540
Kankichi Ryotsu.

175
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:19,231
I won't let the Chief's scheme
go exactly as he planned!

176
00:09:19,281 --> 00:09:20,880
Here, I have to steel my heart and be cruel.

177
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,600
What on earth do you think you're doing?

178
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:29,140
Sneaking into a single man's
room first thing in the morning

179
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:31,020
and cleaning and doing the
laundry without permission.

180
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:32,960
Don't you think that's shameless?

181
00:09:37,540 --> 00:09:40,760
Ryo-sama, do you dislike me?

182
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:45,020
No, that's not really it.

183
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:46,480
So you like me, then?

184
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:49,060
Maria is so happy!

185
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:51,120
Huh?

186
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:52,940
Huh?

187
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,220
That's not what I'm saying.

188
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:58,220
Let me make this clear.

189
00:09:58,220 --> 00:10:01,100
I have no intention of marrying you.

190
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:02,360
W-what... no way...

191
00:10:13,180 --> 00:10:14,800
This is it, this is good enough.

192
00:10:16,540 --> 00:10:17,240
Chief!

193
00:10:19,060 --> 00:10:20,920
Chief! That's just cruel!

194
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,820
Toying with someone's heart like that...

195
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:24,620
What are you talking about?

196
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:27,420
You set a trap to get me married,
didn't you?

197
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:30,340
So you figured it out.

198
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:34,080
I did come up with a plan to marry you off,

199
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:36,040
but the other party turned it down.

200
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:37,500
Here, this is the woman.

201
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,600
Then what about Maria?

202
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:50,480
Well, I'm a huge, damn idiot.

203
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:00,520
Master Ryo

204
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:06,660
About what we talked about this morning,

205
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:15,160
I was thinking maybe I could reconsider it.

206
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:20,380
If it's with you,
maybe I could even consider marriage.

207
00:12:21,020 --> 00:12:21,840
Just kidding.

208
00:12:26,740 --> 00:12:27,620
Master Ryo

209
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:31,580
I'm so happy.

210
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:32,780
I see.

211
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:41,260
Well, I'm off, Maria.

212
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:43,100
We'll be waiting for your return.

213
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:46,880
Just as I thought.

214
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:50,260
The moment he's set to marry,
he suddenly gets serious, they say.

215
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:55,160
Before, no one could imagine him going out
on his own to handle residents' complaints.

216
00:12:55,160 --> 00:12:58,720
Now I can proudly play matchmaker,
as they say.

217
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:08,520
Are you all right?

218
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:14,720
This is...

219
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:19,080
Asado Ryuji, you were a huge
fan of the senior, weren't you?

220
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:20,600
Really?

221
00:13:21,660 --> 00:13:24,400
Yes, I often went to watch
his matches with him too.

222
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:25,220
I'm so happy!

223
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:29,380
Ryu-sama, you've been watching over me all this time,
haven't you?

224
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:32,100
We must have been bound together
by the red thread of fate.

225
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,060
What are you talking about, Maria-san?

226
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:40,500
This Asado Ryuji is my younger brother,
a kickboxer.

227
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:41,960
That's why it's me.

228
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:45,180
That's my ring name.

229
00:13:59,580 --> 00:14:03,900
Asado Ryuji,
the undefeated champion with a 50-0 record

230
00:14:04,460 --> 00:14:07,000
his signature move is the
aerial flying knee strike.

231
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:08,780
But last winter,

232
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:11,500
he suddenly vanished and
has been missing ever since.

233
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:14,760
But I never imagined he'd turn into a woman!

234
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:17,280
Now that you mention it,
she does look a bit like him.

235
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:21,660
Why on earth did he end up like that?

236
00:14:22,460 --> 00:14:25,260
I had someone I truly loved.

237
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:27,180
His name was Gantetsu Iwao,

238
00:14:27,180 --> 00:14:29,040
and he was a kickboxing coach.

239
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:30,480
I love him, I love him so much

240
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:33,740
and finally I decided to become his bride.

241
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:35,820
So that's why you quit kickboxing.

242
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:36,440
Yes.

243
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,680
After all sorts of training,
I finally became the way I am now.

244
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:43,140
But fate turned out to be tragic.

245
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:46,220
My coach went abroad.

246
00:14:46,220 --> 00:14:49,020
Wait, does that coach look like Ryo-chan?

247
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:52,980
Yes, he's exactly like him.
He's my ideal type.

248
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:55,680
So you fell for him at first sight?

249
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:59,980
Was I about to pull off
a wedding between two men?

250
00:15:01,540 --> 00:15:03,780
I'm back from Puzzle.

251
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:06,260
Welcome back, Ryo-sama.

252
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,640
Maria was lonely without you, Ryo-sama.

253
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:11,780
Smooch smooch, yocchi yocchi.

254
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:15,840
Normally, it'd be a heartwarming sight,

255
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:17,980
but after hearing that story just now...

256
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:20,580
Ta-da! Look, Chief!

257
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:23,740
If we get this signed and submitted,

258
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:26,320
Maria and I will officially
be husband and wife.

259
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:26,940
I'm so happy!

260
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:29,940
We need a witness,
so I'm counting on you, Nakagawa, Reiko.

261
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:31,740
I see.

262
00:15:31,740 --> 00:15:32,720
Sorry, lucky you.

263
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:33,620
Really, really.

264
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:36,520
The man who's going to be her husband?

265
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,100
That's me, then.

266
00:15:38,680 --> 00:15:39,940
What are we going to do?

267
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:42,240
We need to tell her the truth quickly.

268
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:45,580
But even if we're the ones to tell her,

269
00:15:46,060 --> 00:15:48,920
Ryotsu.

270
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:51,120
Maria is actually a man.

271
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:53,340
Just kidding.

272
00:15:53,340 --> 00:15:56,320
If you're going to lie,
at least make it more believable.

273
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:59,720
Could it be that you're jealous

274
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:00,700
of me marrying such a beauty?

275
00:16:01,220 --> 00:16:03,900
Soon I'll flaunt our hot newlywed home

276
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:06,500
and make you even more jealous.

277
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:12,540
Being called "Mrs. Ryotsu" is the best.

278
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:15,460
At a time like this,
it's best to hear it from her own mouth.

279
00:16:15,460 --> 00:16:17,560
Are you really going to
make a girl say it herself?

280
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:19,420
Maria's a man, remember?

281
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:20,280
Right.

282
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:21,960
What am I supposed to do?

283
00:16:21,960 --> 00:16:22,600
Can you manage it?

284
00:16:23,460 --> 00:16:25,320
Then just have her talk back, okay?

285
00:16:25,900 --> 00:16:27,600
Once she pulls that out, it's game over.

286
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:28,340
I know.

287
00:16:29,060 --> 00:16:30,880
Ryotsu, how about some tea?

288
00:16:30,880 --> 00:16:31,620
Whoa!

289
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:34,317
S-sorry.

290
00:16:34,367 --> 00:16:37,240
I didn't mean any harm, though.

291
00:16:37,340 --> 00:16:39,620
At this rate,
there's no way we can submit it today.

292
00:16:40,340 --> 00:16:41,120
It's fine.

293
00:16:42,460 --> 00:16:45,220
Just in case something like this happened,
I brought a spare.

294
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:47,760
Good.

295
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:50,800
Ryotsu...

296
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:52,460
Watch out! It's Ryotsu's cloud!

297
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:53,380
Found it! Found it!

298
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:53,920
Argh!

299
00:16:57,640 --> 00:17:00,420
Looks like it was just an ordinary cloud,
Susuman.

300
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:01,920
I didn't mean any harm.

301
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:02,940
It's all right.

302
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:05,360
We still have a spare.

303
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:09,180
Whoa, how many did you bring?

304
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:13,240
Hey, so that it's more certain
than my marriage to Maria,

305
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:16,460
I brought marriage registration
forms for everyone at the station.

306
00:17:17,220 --> 00:17:17,940
Yay!

307
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:20,560
Haah...

308
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:29,020
There's no other way. Ryotsu, I need to talk to you.
What is it?
From now on, you're the contracting party.

309
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:30,160
Just come here.

310
00:17:36,060 --> 00:17:43,920
What's with the sudden seriousness about marriage?
Just the other day you were telling me to get married right away!

311
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:47,960
Don't tell me you've lost the
nerve to go through with it.

312
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:49,700
That's not it.

313
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:53,500
I'm saying you shouldn't
decide on marriage on a whim.

314
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:55,260
You may not know this,

315
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:58,940
but there's a saying that
marriage is the grave of life.

316
00:17:58,940 --> 00:18:01,560
That might be a grave in your case, Chief,

317
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:04,920
but for Maria and me,
it'll definitely be heaven.

318
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:07,300
It'll definitely turn into hell.

319
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:09,280
Once you find out Maria's true identity.

320
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:15,160
You shouldn't judge a
spouse by appearance alone.

321
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,480
Getting to know what's
inside them matters too.

322
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:20,340
You know Maria has a
good personality, Chief.

323
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:22,160
Not that kind of inside.

324
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:30,020
What I mean is, before the wedding, you should go to
a hot spring at least once and bathe in the same bath.

325
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:33,120
Maria goes in the women's bath! There's no way you two can bathe together,
come on.

326
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:34,780
Well, that's...

327
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:36,800
Could it be, Chief?

328
00:18:37,420 --> 00:18:38,420
You caught on?

329
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:44,480
While Maria's bathing happily in the open-air bath, I'll sneak in too.
That's my scheme!

330
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:50,320
Let me in too! Your friendship is pretty indecent,
isn't it?

331
00:18:51,980 --> 00:19:02,260
Normally I think things through to the point of annoyance, so why do I fail to notice at times like this?
What I'm saying is that bathing together might lead to a discovery beyond what you'd expect.

332
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:03,880
Whoa! An unexpected discovery?

333
00:19:04,300 --> 00:19:07,812
Yes! Unexpected, very unexpected, something
astonishing that will make you gasp!

334
00:19:07,862 --> 00:19:12,280
We might discover something so unexpected it's beyond unexpected!
Unexpected indeed!

335
00:19:12,600 --> 00:19:12,880
Aaaaah!

336
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:13,580
Maria!

337
00:19:15,960 --> 00:19:16,660
Ken-chan!

338
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:27,220
These guys are sold as
villain wrestlers back home.

339
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:29,098
If you resist recklessly,

340
00:19:29,148 --> 00:19:32,640
you'll end up getting
put to sleep like this guy.

341
00:19:33,150 --> 00:19:36,300
Now, you're going to keep us
company for a good long while.

342
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:39,460
Hey! What do you think
you're doing to my Maria!

343
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:40,580
Joe-sama!

344
00:19:40,780 --> 00:19:42,780
It's you again! Everyone, take him out!

345
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:55,280
That George guy is really intimidating.

346
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:11,740
Now's the time,
just make it a marriage registration!

347
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Ryo-sama

348
00:20:18,600 --> 00:20:20,300
Don't let him get away, or you're dead meat!

349
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:27,520
Anyone who lays a hand on Ryo-sama,
I won't forgive!

350
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:36,000
As expected of a former kickboxing champion.

351
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:38,860
Laying a hand on Ryo-sama? Not a chance!

352
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:47,280
What?

353
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:53,800
That's...

354
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:56,420
Asado Ryuji's finishing move

355
00:20:56,420 --> 00:20:58,760
Aerial flying knee strike!

356
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:04,020
How could Maria pull off that move

357
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:07,480
Ryo-sama

358
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:12,020
Ryo-sama, are you all right?

359
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,220
What's this... a cushion?

360
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:16,400
What is this?

361
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:19,020
Something squishy is hitting my head!

362
00:21:19,540 --> 00:21:20,520
No way, this is...

363
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:23,860
No...

364
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:30,040
What is it, Maria?

365
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:31,740
What's that thing on your... cushion?

366
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:34,280
How embarrassing.

367
00:21:34,280 --> 00:21:36,400
It's something you have too, Ryo-sama.

368
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:38,900
Then what about your chest?

369
00:21:39,500 --> 00:21:41,260
There's a seam showing.

370
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:45,880
So Maria is a man!

371
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:57,800
Looks like you finally understand.

372
00:21:57,800 --> 00:22:01,600
I would have liked to make
you understand in a gentler way.

373
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:03,240
It can't be helped.

374
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:06,920
Ryo-sama! You came to rescue me, didn't you?

375
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:10,600
I'm so happy!
Our love really is eternal, darling.

376
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:13,720
When shall we have the wedding?
What about the honeymoon?

377
00:22:15,620 --> 00:22:16,840
Don't be ridiculous!

378
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:19,640
Why on earth would I have to marry you!

379
00:22:19,760 --> 00:22:24,240
But you signed the marriage registration
form saying you'd consider marrying me!

380
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:26,980
At that time, I thought you were a woman.

381
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:29,500
I have no intention of marrying a man!

382
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:38,920
Even though you finally met that person,

383
00:22:43,120 --> 00:22:50,020
that's a bit pitiful, isn't it.

384
00:22:50,440 --> 00:22:52,240
Making a girl cry like that is cruel.

385
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:53,760
He's a man, dammit!

386
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:56,540
I want to cry too, I really do!

387
00:22:57,720 --> 00:23:02,020
But at least we've been spared from having
to cry through a wedding between two men.

388
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:08,640
I wonder what Maria's doing right now.

389
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:10,740
So you're still worried about it?

390
00:23:11,100 --> 00:23:13,020
You should have just gone
through with the marriage.

391
00:23:13,020 --> 00:23:14,380
Don't be an idiot!

392
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:17,040
It's just that we parted
on such a bitter note,

393
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:18,760
and it's bugging me a little, that's all.

394
00:23:19,620 --> 00:23:21,240
I hope it didn't turn
into a night view scene.

395
00:23:26,660 --> 00:23:27,900
Yo!

396
00:23:29,080 --> 00:23:30,340
What do you want, you punks?

397
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:36,180
Today I'm showing the new
officer around our jurisdiction.

398
00:23:36,620 --> 00:23:37,840
Come on, come down here.

399
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:50,260
Ryo-sama

400
00:23:50,260 --> 00:23:52,720
I couldn't forget you, Ryo-sama,

401
00:23:52,720 --> 00:23:55,360
so I became a police officer so
I could stay by your side forever.

402
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:58,040
A woman's obsession is a terrifying thing.

403
00:23:58,040 --> 00:23:59,560
Maria's a man, you know!

404
00:24:04,140 --> 00:24:06,200
That Maria was a man all along!

405
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:08,820
I was about to get married so quickly,
wasn't I?

406
00:24:09,340 --> 00:24:11,140
But then, targeting that very Maria,

407
00:24:11,140 --> 00:24:13,320
a mysterious group of
martial artists attacked.

408
00:24:13,320 --> 00:24:15,580
Damn you, using such weird swordsmanship!

409
00:24:15,580 --> 00:24:17,280
Who the hell are you guys?

410
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:20,160
Next time: shocking,
direct hit, book-filled!

411
00:24:20,520 --> 00:24:21,240
Nice to meet you.

412
00:24:30,540 --> 00:24:37,100
They gossip that I'm a
woman who can't fall in love,

413
00:24:37,100 --> 00:24:43,000
but I have a mountain
of things I want to do.

414
00:24:44,400 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride a motorbike
across a harsh desert.

415
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,200
I want to be freer than a bird.

416
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:07,120
Dreams that change as
fast as a kaleidoscope.

417
00:25:08,820 --> 00:25:15,280
Sorry, my heart in love, wait for me.

418
00:25:15,280 --> 00:25:22,200
Panorama of the future,
the dazzle will come soon enough.

419
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:26,502
You understand, right?

420
00:25:26,552 --> 00:25:30,100
Sorry, wait for me.

